From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0338-nemyu-01-written-native-bindings-keep-stated-size.patch

Source: 0338-nemyu-01-written-native-bindings-keep-stated-size.patch
Moved by hand: the cut sits inside upstream's binding cache lambda (0066); a native pointer's size word is read there, the cache key does not carry it

buffer_cache: EDEN_NX2_SSBO_WRITES_SIZED=1 keeps a written native binding at its stated size

Rule from notquiteog/Elysium 1656cee4d8 (branch main, merge of zortos293/Lichii bisect/oot-6):
native reads use the mapping, native writes keep descriptor sizing, "so both the grass fix and
the MKW pacing fix hold". The fault it answers: Nemyu 6605d298 (Uesleizito Zin, gitlab.com/
nemyu-emulator/nemyu, branch nemyu, tag nemyu-v0.1.4) and upstream PR 609 (Mcm190). GPL-3.0-or-later,
as the core.

Upstream #535 (2e12e0def5) sizes every native compute storage buffer from its mapping, up to 8 MiB.
A written binding is marked GPU-written whole. Our pin e736dfde9e has that: it sits after the revert
4bc1ede493 of #561 and before #571 put #561 back. 0082 already stops the worst of it. Nemyu's own
table, RTX 3050 laptop, so only the order carries over:

  mapped                       57-73 ms a race frame
  mapped + exact preflush      29.5, 30.8 ms    <- our tree (0082)
  descriptor sizing            22.4, 22.5 ms
  descriptor + exact preflush  21.5, 21.1 ms    <- with rebase-03

rebase-03 (EDEN_NX2_SSBO_DLSS_ONLY=1) also cuts read bindings. This one cuts only written ones:
reads keep the mapping, tables and DLSS passes are untouched. Nothing here makes a binding larger.
Its worst case, if the word after the pointer is not a size: a written binding ends early, so writes
past that point are dropped and reads through the same binding past it return 0. The table above
sizes every binding, reads too; nothing has measured this written-only rule.

=1 cuts. =2 changes nothing and only logs what =1 would cut, so a normal run can count it. Unset
is the old behaviour. With rebase-03 at =1 this has little left to do; the two stack. InDlssEvaluation
is rebase-03's IsDlssDispatch under its own name so that each patch stands alone.

Core patch. Nothing here has run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 1e28e49712..74d02bd325 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -871,6 +871,23 @@ void BufferCache<P>::BindComputeStorageBuffer(size_t ssbo_index, u32 cbuf_index,
 
     const auto& cbufs = launch_desc.const_buffer_config;
     GPUVAddr ssbo_addr = cbufs[cbuf_index].Address() + cbuf_offset;
+    // EDEN_NX2_SSBO_WRITES_SIZED=1: a written binding of a direct native pointer keeps the size in
+    // the word after the pointer; read bindings, tables and DLSS passes keep their mappings. A
+    // written binding is marked GPU-written whole, so one of up to 8 MiB marks data the program
+    // never touched: Mario Kart World read back gigabytes a second (upstream #609). Nemyu's races
+    // ran 30 ms a frame, 21 with every binding sized, reads too. =2 only logs what =1 would cut.
+    static const u8 writes_sized = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_SSBO_WRITES_SIZED");
+        return static_cast<u8>(value == nullptr ? 0 : value[0] == '1' ? 1 : value[0] == '2' ? 2 : 0);
+    }();
+    native_written_binding_mode =
+        is_written && indirect_offset == ~0U && kepler_compute->IsNativeMode() &&
+                !kepler_compute->InDlssEvaluation()
+            ? writes_sized
+            : u8{0};
+    SCOPE_EXIT {
+        native_written_binding_mode = 0;
+    };
     if (indirect_offset != ~0U) {
         // The pointer is an entry of a table the constant buffer points to.
         const GPUVAddr holder = gpu_memory->Read<u64>(ssbo_addr);
@@ -3289,6 +3306,30 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
             }
             return (std::min)(memory_layout_size, static_cast<u32>(8_MiB));
         }();
+        if (native_written_binding_mode != 0) {
+            // A native pointer's size word is read here only (the binding cache above keys native
+            // answers without it, so a stated size that changes under the same page table is seen
+            // at the next page table change).
+            const u64 stated_qword = reads_size_word ? next_qword : gpu_memory->Read<u64>(ssbo_addr + 8);
+            const u32 stated_size = static_cast<u32>(stated_qword);
+            if (static_cast<u32>(stated_qword >> 32) == 0 && stated_size != 0 && stated_size < size) {
+                // Runs on one thread; the log thins out as the count doubles.
+                static u64 cut_bindings{};
+                static u64 cut_bytes{};
+                ++cut_bindings;
+                cut_bytes += size - stated_size;
+                if ((cut_bindings & (cut_bindings - 1)) == 0) {
+                    LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                             "Native written bindings cut to their stated size: {} so far, {} MiB "
+                             "fewer bytes marked; last {} to {} bytes (mode {})",
+                             cut_bindings, cut_bytes >> 20, size, stated_size,
+                             native_written_binding_mode);
+                }
+                if (native_written_binding_mode == 1) {
+                    size = stated_size;
+                }
+            }
+        }
         if (native_pointer && size != 0) {
             // Stop where the mapping or its device range does: the binding is one device range, and
             // a written one isn't split into separate ranges without sparse sources.
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
index 966d7a5833..87969143db 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
@@ -453,6 +453,9 @@ public:
         u64 size{};
         u64 removals{~u64{0}};
     };
+    /// EDEN_NX2_SSBO_WRITES_SIZED: the compute binding being made is written through a direct
+    /// native pointer. 1 keeps the size the word after the pointer states, 2 only counts it.
+    u8 native_written_binding_mode{};
     std::array<Nx2RecentRange, 8> nx2_recent_gpu_ranges{};
     std::array<Nx2RecentRange, 8> nx2_recent_uncommitted_ranges{};
     size_t nx2_recent_gpu_next{};
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
index eca391240f..19cdf5c082 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
@@ -259,6 +259,11 @@ public:
     /// are emulated: in a game DLSS evaluation when the game's own network may draw, and always
     /// for Donkey Kong Bananza.
     [[nodiscard]] bool EmulatesNativeTensorPrograms() const;
+    /// Whether the dispatch being run belongs to a game DLSS evaluation, whose storage pointers
+    /// are followed by parameters, not sizes.
+    [[nodiscard]] bool InDlssEvaluation() const {
+        return native_mode && dlss_chain.active;
+    }
 
